<title>UK: Mexico prices $1.0 billion 10-year bond, +335 b.p..</title>
<headline>Mexico prices $1.0 billion 10-year bond, +335 b.p..</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico has given a 9.875 percent coupon and par issue/reoffer price to its $1.0 billion 10-year bond to yield 335 basis points over U.S. Treasuries, joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and Salomon Brothers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Wednesday.</p>
